drm/msm/dp: notify the connector unconditionally on HPD

msm_dp_display_send_hpd_event() calls drm_helper_hpd_irq_event(), which
re-probes every connector on the device and only emits a uevent for the ones
whose detected status changed.

msm_dp_bridge_detect() derives the connector status from link_ready, and
msm_dp_display_send_hpd_notification() sets link_ready before calling this
function. A userspace probe that lands in that window sees the new status and
updates the cached connector status itself, so by the time
drm_helper_hpd_irq_event() runs there is no change left to report and the
uevent is dropped.

Losing that event is not cosmetic, because msm_dp_bridge_atomic_check()
returns -ENOTCONN while link_ready is false. On a Fairphone 5, unplugging and
replugging a DP dock reproduces it:

  [drm:drm_sysfs_connector_hotplug_event] [CONNECTOR:38:DP-1] generating connector hotplug event
  [drm:msm_dp_bridge_atomic_check] link_ready = false
  [drm:drm_atomic_check_only] atomic driver check for 00000000fcb163f8 failed: -107
  [drm:msm_dp_bridge_atomic_check] link_ready = false
  [drm:drm_atomic_check_only] atomic driver check for 00000000fcb163f8 failed: -107
  [drm:dpu_crtc_atomic_check] crtc71 -> enable 0, active 0, skip atomic_check
  [drm:msm_dp_bridge_detect] link_ready = true

The compositor commits against a connector that is not link-ready yet, gets
-ENOTCONN, disables the CRTC, and is never told that the link came up 51 ms
later. The connector is left reporting connected with no CRTC attached, and
the external display stays dark until the DRM master is replaced -- stopping
the compositor, or shutting down, lights it up again via fbdev.

Use drm_kms_helper_connector_hotplug_event() so the event is delivered for
this connector whether or not a racing probe already observed the new status.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <drm/display/drm_dp_aux_bus.h>
 #include <drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_edid.h>
+#include <drm/drm_probe_helper.h>
 
 #include "msm_drv.h"
 #include "msm_kms.h"
@@ -352,7 +353,17 @@ static void msm_dp_display_send_hpd_event(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display)
 	dp = container_of(msm_dp_display, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
 	connector = dp->msm_dp_display.connector;
-	drm_helper_hpd_irq_event(connector->dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * Do not use drm_helper_hpd_irq_event() here: it re-probes the
+	 * connector and only emits a uevent if the detected status changed.
+	 * ->detect() is derived from link_ready, which has already been
+	 * updated by the caller, so a userspace probe racing this call latches
+	 * the new status first and the event is then suppressed -- leaving a
+	 * client that failed its modeset with -ENOTCONN with nothing to retry
+	 * on. Notify unconditionally instead.
+	 */
+	drm_kms_helper_connector_hotplug_event(connector);
 }
 
 static int msm_dp_display_send_hpd_notification(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp,
